3. **Keep execution with one owner.** The agent owning the execute-and-verify phase performs sequential and tightly coupled actions locally. Delegate only bounded work that materially benefits from independent context or parallel execution; implementation uses EXEC, read-only collection uses READ, and independent design review uses PLAN (conventions §10.8). Do not hand an action through another implementation layer merely to repeat the same EXEC assignment. Give each delegate the narrow brief in `references/agent_dispatch_spec.md`; the phase owner integrates results and verifies inspectable original command/result evidence, re-running only stale, missing or integration-affected checks. The action-start snapshots and failure rules in that reference also bind local execution and preserve pre-existing work and raw evidence.
